            "\\paragraph{Results.} Table~\\ref{mctest_results} shows the experiment results on MCTest.  Both \\contextmodel~and \\standardentail$_{\\mathrm{DocNLI}}$ rely on the indirect supervision from DocNLI, but \\contextmodel~outperforms \\standardentail$_{\\mathrm{DocNLI}}$ on both MC160 and MC500, achieving the new SOTA performance. \\parallelmodel~performs worse than \\contextmodel~because it is more comparable with the \\standardentail$_{\\mathrm{vanilla}}$:  both use the RoBERTa-large encoder and do not pretrain on extra data. Nevertheless, \\parallelmodel~achieves multi-option joint training, which leads to the improvement by  large margins: 81.25 vs. 42.50 on MC160, and 82.50 vs. 63.67 on MC500.\n",
